    "final_answer": "I have found the answer. Looking at the Stats page for LeBron James on ESPN, the \"Regular Season Averages\" table clearly shows his career totals.\n\n## Answer\n\nAccording to ESPN's Stats page for LeBron James, he has played **1,622 games** in his career (Regular Season), with 1,620 games started.\n\n**Key Career Stats (Regular Season):**\n- **Games Played (GP):** 1,622\n- **Games Started (GS):** 1,620\n- **Minutes Per Game:** 37.6\n- **Points Per Game:** 26.8\n- **Field Goal %:** 50.7\n- **Rebounds Per Game:** 7.5\n- **Assists Per Game:** 7.4\n\nThe stats span his career from 2003-04 (Cleveland Cavaliers) through the 2025-26 season, including his time with the Cleveland Cavaliers, Miami Heat, and Los Angeles Lakers. Note that ESPN currently lists him as a member of the Philadelphia 76ers for the upcoming 2026-27 season, though his career totals reflect games played through the end of the 2025-26 season.",
